#Feature asbsorption - i.e that lesser components steal credit from more general ones.
Sparse autoencoders can appear to encode a general feature, but under sparsity, other more specific latents take over some inputs, “absorbing” them. This causes the general latent to miss cases, giving high precision but low recall and limiting interpretability.
